MINISTER FOR TOURISM AND CULTURE <br><br>(SMT. AMBIKA SONI)
<br><br>(a)	Majuli Island, Assam and Kalka-Shimla Railway were considered by UNESCO for inscription on the World Heritage List in 2008, based on nomination dossiers sent earlier, under the “cultural landscape”, and ‘cultural heritage’ categories respectively. While Kalka Shimla Railway has been inscribed, a decision on Majuli Island was deferred. 
Nominations to be made in 2009 are under consideration. <br><br>(b)to (d) While deferring a decision on Majuli Island, the World Heritage Committee of UNESCO  recommended the following actions:- a)	Assemble a complete inventory of the 31 surviving Sattras on the island as a preliminary to considering which Sattras might have the potential to demonstrate  Outstanding Universal  Value and be nominated as the property;
b)  Allow an ICOMOS evaluation mission to visit the property to consider the extent and scope of the Sattras; 
c)  Undertake an appraisal of the overall river basin in which Majuli lies and the potential impact of upstream development, deforestation and the building of dams, in order to ascertain whether managed retreat is the only realistic approach to the flooding and erosion processes
A fresh nomination dossier is required to be prepared by an inter-disciplinary team taking into account the recommendations of the World Heritage Committee. At this stage, it is not possible to indicate a definite time frame for renominating Majuli Island
